{
  "sn6.3:0.1": "Linked Discourses 6.3 ",
  "sn6.3:0.2": "1. The Appeal ",
  "sn6.3:0.3": "With Brahmadeva ",
  "sn6.3:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "sn6.3:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. ",
  "sn6.3:1.3": "Now at that time a certain brahmin lady had a son named Brahmadeva, who had gone forth from the lay life to homelessness in the presence of the Buddha. ",
  "sn6.3:2.1": "Then Venerable Brahmadeva, living alone, withdrawn, diligent, keen, and resolute, soon realized the supreme culmination of the spiritual path in this very life. He lived having achieved with his own insight the goal for which gentlemen rightly go forth from the lay life to homelessness. ",
  "sn6.3:2.2": "He understood: “Rebirth is ended; the spiritual journey has been completed; what had to be done has been done; there is nothing further for this place.” ",
  "sn6.3:2.3": "And Venerable Brahmadeva became one of the perfected. ",
  "sn6.3:3.1": "Then Brahmadeva robed up in the morning and, taking his bowl and robe, entered Sāvatthī for alms. ",
  "sn6.3:3.2": "Wandering indiscriminately for almsfood in Sāvatthī, he approached his own mother’s home. ",
  "sn6.3:3.3": "Now at that time Brahmadeva’s mother, the brahmin lady, was presenting a regular oblation to the Divinity. ",
  "sn6.3:3.4": "Then the divinity Sahampati thought, ",
  "sn6.3:3.5": "“This Venerable Brahmadeva’s mother, the brahmin lady, offers up a regular oblation to the Divinity. ",